# Build artifacts
workspace/
dist/
*.img
*.img.xz
*.zip
*.tmp

# Generated files from JSON config
# Generated variant configs: generate.py rewrites these before every build
# (scripts/build.sh:38), so committing them only guarantees version drift -
# semantic-release bumps config/variants/*.json without regenerating them.
src/variants/*/config
src/modules/*/filesystem/root/opt/bgrpiimage/

# CustomPiOS drops the custompios_path sidecar at build time
src/custompios_path
src/workspace/
src/workspace-*/
src/build.log

# Cached base image downloads (.img.xz and extracted .img)
src/image-cache/

# CustomPiOS config.local is generated by scripts/build.sh at build time
src/config.local

# tools/requirements.txt is auto-synced from scripts/requirements.txt by
# the run.* launchers before docker build - so it drifts on every run.
tools/requirements.txt

# CustomPiOS is cloned at build time into this path
CustomPiOS/
!CustomPiOS/.keep

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Secrets (just in case)
.env
.env.local
secrets.json

# Local key material for release signing - PRIVATE halves only.
#
# The whole directory rather than an extension allowlist: a folder named
# .secrets is a working area for key material, and an allowlist is one
# forgotten suffix away from a committed private key.
#
# The PUBLIC half deliberately does NOT live here. It is committed at
# src/modules/bgrpiimage-base/filesystem/root/usr/share/bgrpiimage/trusted-keys.d/
# because it has two jobs that both require it to be in git: it ships into
# the image as the trust anchor devices verify releases against, and it is
# the only way to check which key CI signs with - a private key cannot be
# read back out of Actions secrets, so the committed public half is the
# reference. scripts/push-secrets.py refuses to upload a private key whose
# public counterpart is missing or does not match.
#
# Private keys reach GitHub Actions secrets through scripts/push-secrets.py
# and never leave this machine any other way.
.secrets/

# Belt and braces: no private key may be committed from anywhere in the tree,
# whatever it is called or wherever someone drops it. Nothing tracked matches
# these today.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
.claude/
